<p><code>pop-code</code> writes PHP. You build a class, function or enum out of generator objects, and render it to
a string or a file. The same component reads in the other direction: reflection turns existing code
back into those generator objects, so you can add a method to a class that already exists and write it
out again. This is what scaffolding tools are built from — <code>pop-kettle</code> generates its controllers and
models this way.</p>
